About the Company: &nbsp; 

LIQVID English Edge Pvt. Ltd. is a leading digital learning solutions company focused on English language training, communication skills, and corporate learning. We deliver e-learning content, LMS platforms, and customized training programs for diverse clients. &nbsp; 

Job Description - Azure Cloud / DevOps Engineer&nbsp; 

Experience: 3-5 Years&nbsp; 

Employment Type: Full-Time&nbsp; &nbsp; 

Location: Noida&nbsp; &nbsp; 

Department: Technology / Infrastructure&nbsp; 

Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in computer science, Information Technology, Engineering, or&nbsp; 

&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; a related field preferred. &nbsp; 

Budget for candidate - 6 to 9 Lacs Per Annum. &nbsp; 

About the Role&nbsp; 

We are looking for a hands-on Azure Cloud / DevOps Engineer to manage Azure infrastructure, Linux servers, CI/CD pipelines, deployment automation, monitoring, security, backups, and production troubleshooting across Development, UAT/Staging, and Production environments. 

Key Responsibilities

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Manage Azure resources including VMs, App Services, Storage, MySQL, VNets, Subnets, NSGs, DNS, and Load Balancers. 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Administer Linux/Ubuntu servers, including Nginx/Apache, users, permissions, services, disks, logs, and SSL certificates. 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Build and maintain Git/GitHub and GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines; automate deployments, releases, and rollbacks. 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Monitor infrastructure and applications using Azure Monitor and Application Insights. 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Troubleshoot server, application, networking, database, DNS, SSL, and deployment issues. 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Implement cloud security controls, RBAC, firewall rules, SSH security, secrets management, and server hardening. 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Manage backups, restore activities, and disaster recovery; coordinate with Development and QA teams. 

Required Skills Mandatory: &nbsp; 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Microsoft Azure: VM, App Service, Storage, MySQL, VNet, NSG, RBAC, Azure Monitor, and Backup. 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Linux/Ubuntu administration; Nginx/Apache; Git/GitHub and GitHub Actions. 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CI/CD and deployment automation; networking fundamentals (TCP/IP, DNS, HTTP/HTTPS, SSL/TLS, firewall, VPN, subnets). 

·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Basic Bash, PowerShell, or Python scripting; production troubleshooting and incident management. 

Good to Have: &nbsp; 

Terraform/Ansible; Docker/Kubernetes/AKS; Azure Key Vault/Application Gateway; Azure DevOps; AWS fundamentals (EC2, S3, RDS, VPC, IAM); cloud cost optimization and security hardening. 

Qualifications & Certifications

A bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related field is preferred. Microsoft Azure Administrator Associate (AZ-104) and Azure DevOps Engineer Expert (AZ-400) are preferred, but certifications are not mandatory; practical Azure experience takes priority. 

Candidate Profile&nbsp; 

