About the Role&nbsp; 

DoctusTech builds AI agents for value-based care organizations, covering HCC risk adjustment, &nbsp; coding compliance, HEDIS, and clinical documentation. &nbsp; 

This is a hands-on role. You will personally review AI outputs against medical records, quantify&nbsp; accuracy, build the models that measure clinical and financial impact, and give engineering&nbsp; precise, evidence-backed feedback. You will be the clinical quality gate before anything ships to&nbsp; customers. &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

Clinical QA of AI Outputs&nbsp; 

• Review AI-generated HCC suggestions, compliance flags, and documentation outputs&nbsp; against source records, line by line. &nbsp; 

• Validate each diagnosis against MEAT criteria, diagnostic status (active vs. history), and&nbsp; current coding guidelines. &nbsp; 

• Build and maintain gold-standard chart sets used to test agent performance. • Score agent outputs for precision, recall, and false positive rate, and track trends across&nbsp; releases. &nbsp; 

• Identify error patterns and write clear, reproducible defect reports for engineering and&nbsp; data science. &nbsp; 

• Sign off on clinical quality before releases. &nbsp; 

Risk Adjustment Analysis&nbsp; 

• Apply CMS-HCC V28 logic, including hierarchies, interaction terms, and RAF&nbsp; calculation. &nbsp; 

• Assess RADV exposure on sampled charts: unsupported HCCs, error rates, and&nbsp; financial impact. &nbsp; 

• Track CMS model and rule changes and translate them into product requirements. &nbsp; 

Excel Modeling & Reporting&nbsp; 

